[b]Drag and drop techs in your research queue to reorder them. A tech's queued prerequisites move with it, so the queue stays in a valid order.[/b]

No more removing half your tech queue and adding it back to research one thing first. It only uses the game's own queue commands, no cheating.

[img]GIF_URL_HERE[/img]

[h2]How it works[/h2]
[list]
[*]Drag a tech along the queue row above the tech tree. Drop it on another tech, or in the gap between two.
[*]Drop a queued tech on the current research to research it now. The old one becomes next in line. Drag the current research into the queue to put it off.
[*]Drag a tech ahead of something it needs, and that prerequisite comes along, just in front of it. Drag a prerequisite behind a tech that needs it, and that tech follows. A short message says so when a tech can't land exactly where you dropped it.
[*][b]+N[/b] opens the rest of the queue as a second row, so you can drag those techs too. Their arrow button moves them straight to the front.
[*]Research progress is kept: a moved tech keeps every point already spent on it.
[*]Clicking, shift-clicking and the X button work as before. The mod moves techs with those same commands.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Victoria 3 version 1.15.[/b]
[*][b]Achievement compatible.[/b]
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] Add or remove it mid-campaign; it stores nothing in your save.
[*][b]Single-player.[/b] Untested in multiplayer.
[*][b]All eleven languages Victoria 3 ships.[/b] The only text is one tooltip and one short message, using the game's own words for research queue and technology.
[*][b]Conflicts:[/b] it replaces the tech panel and the queued tech icon, so another mod changing those, or the number of techs the row shows, clashes.
[*][b]Tech mods:[/b] techs added by another mod can be dragged down the queue, not up, and the arrow button ignores them. A tech dragged down past one of them takes it along. Mods that change the base game's tech prerequisites are not supported yet.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Post a comment if something breaks, especially with other mods. A thumbs up below the screenshots helps other players find it!
